# Postgres connection string (Neon). On Vercel, connect the Neon integration
# and this will be populated automatically — for local dev, copy the
# connection string from your Neon project dashboard.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://user:password@host/dbname?sslmode=require"

# The single password used to unlock the app at /login.
# Pick something long and memorable — there is no username, just this.
APP_PASSWORD="change-me"

# Optional: only needed for photo uploads on the /gifts page. Enable the
# Vercel Blob integration (Storage -> Blob) and this is set automatically
# on Vercel. For local dev, create a Blob store in the Vercel dashboard and
# copy its read/write token here. Without it, you can still paste a photo
# URL directly instead of uploading a file.
BLOB_READ_WRITE_TOKEN=""

# Optional but recommended: secures the /api/cron/daily route so only Vercel's
# own Cron invocations (and you, with this value) can trigger it. Set any
# random string here and add the same value as an environment variable in
# Vercel — Vercel automatically sends it as a Bearer token to Cron routes
# when CRON_SECRET is set on the project. Without it, the route is open to
# anyone who finds the URL (it only ever reads/writes notifications, no
# destructive action, but a random string costs nothing).
CRON_SECRET=""

# Optional: powers the "similar restaurants nearby" and "new opening" scans
# on the daily cron (Google Places Nearby Search + Place Details, plus
# Geocoding to resolve your partner's city/neighborhood). Get a key from the
# Google Cloud Console with the Places API and Geocoding API enabled. Without
# it, favorite-restaurant check-ins still fire, just without the similar-
# restaurant bundle or new-opening alerts.
GOOGLE_PLACES_API_KEY=""

# Optional but recommended: powers the "paste your notes and we'll sort it
# out" onboarding path, which uses the Claude API to pull structured fields
# (preferences, key dates, sizes, etc.) out of freeform pasted text. Get a
# key from https://console.anthropic.com. Without it, that onboarding path
# still works, it just skips straight to the manual quick-pick questions.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=""
